/-!
# A056230

Construct difference array so that (1) first row begins with 1, (2) every row is monotonic increasing, (3) no number appears more than once, (4) smallest number not yet used begins a new row. Sequence gives array read by antidiagonals.

The 60 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A056230

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 7, 11, 17, 26,
    12, 19, 30, 47, 73, 13, 25, 44, 74, 121,
    194, 14, 27, 52, 96, 170, 291, 485, 15, 29,
